<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zhangjiakou</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Kalgan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zhangjiakou, formerly known as Kalgan, is a city in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebei">Hebei</a> province, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, at a gateway through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-wall-of-china">Great Wall</a> towards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongolia">Mongolia</a>. It long served as a trading centre between China, Mongolia and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, especially for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tea">tea</a> caravans. During the Japanese occupation it was the capital of the Mengjiang government from 1939 to 1945, and it co-hosted the 2022 Winter Olympics.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zhangjiakou.jpg" alt="Zhangjiakou" width="320" height="202" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 黑夜有灯 · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E6%B8%85%E6%B2%B3%E5%B2%B8%E4%B8%8A%E6%98%AF%E6%88%91%E5%AE%B6_-_panoramio.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
